## 0. Resumen en 30 segundos

> 🗣️ "The Group Comparator takes a group name and a reference firewall. It finds that group in every firewall where it exists, compares the full tree (the group and all its nested subgroups) against the reference, and lists every firewall with what is **added** (present here, not in the reference) and what is **missing** (in the reference, not here), per subgroup. It also generates the Playflows `add to` / `rm from` commands to align each firewall, and exports the result to CSV. It reads from the Group Lookup tables of ticket 3637 instead of calling the Playflows API live, so it's fast (a fixed number of queries, independent of how many firewalls) but it shows the data from the last sync."

